WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.275
So, four asks.

2
00:00:01.275 --> 00:00:05.452
Name the owners: the sponsor, the
CISO, the authorizing official,

3
00:00:05.452 --> 00:00:10.575
the identity engineering lead, and someone
who owns the gaps between the tools.

4
00:00:10.575 --> 00:00:12.675
Start read-only discovery now.

5
00:00:12.675 --> 00:00:16.160
It needs no elevated access
to begin, and the request for

6
00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.175
more access then follows the
evidence rather than preceding it.

7
00:00:20.175 --> 00:00:21.663
Put the dates on the plan.

8
00:00:21.663 --> 00:00:26.126
Connect Sync has to be
upgraded by April 7, 2027.

9
00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:32.537
NTLM and legacy authentication should come
off wave by wave, not in one weekend.

10
00:00:32.537 --> 00:00:35.770
And agree what done means:
every control backed by

11
00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:39.238
evidence an assessor can read,
not a status in a ticket.

12
00:00:39.238 --> 00:00:43.500
Identity matters because it is now
where every access decision is made.

13
00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:47.536
Getting it right once, while the
platform is being rebuilt anyway,

14
00:00:47.536 --> 00:00:50.675
is far cheaper than rebuilding
the same gaps twice.

15
00:00:50.675 --> 00:00:54.311
The Federal Modernization
Workbook's Book 02 has the full

16
00:00:54.311 --> 00:00:58.325
argument and the runbooks, with
every external claim footnoted.

17
00:00:58.325 --> 00:01:00.226
Book 03, HR-Driven Identity,

18
00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:04.375
picks up where the facts in
the directory should come from.

19
00:01:04.375 --> 00:01:05.210
Thank you.
